{
  "$description": "MorphScreen's default theme, in the W3C Design Tokens format (DTCG 2025.10): IBM Plex Sans and Mono with a petrol accent (roadmap Q11). Every platform's look comes from this file: `node spec/tokens.ts` writes render/tokens.css, sdk/swift/Sources/MorphScreen/Tokens.swift and sdk/android/ui/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/morphscreen/ui/Tokens.kt, and each SDK reads a theme in this form at run time (applyTheme on the web, Theme.use in SwiftUI, MorphTheme in Compose). color, shadow and heat have one group per mode: light, dark (with the system or when pinned) and mono (grayscale: tones become ink on light grey). Line heights are ratios, as DTCG's typography type has them; the generators round size x ratio to whole pixels. The faces ship inside each SDK under the SIL Open Font License; a theme that names other families uses them when the app has them, else the system face.",
